From 9631f8a9c9946dc6625d53d563c1a50aecfb460c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mario Behn <mario.behn@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 23:22:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/14] Add libiio0: libiio 0.26 for the programs that use the
 0.x API

libiio 1.0 has no 0.x headers and its libiio.so.0 compatibility layer
runs 0.x programs with a different buffer model: SoapyPlutoSDR did not
stream through it (RX stalled, TX could not create its buffer), plutotx
fell back to its low speed buffer mode and the layer prints a banner on
stdout. libad9361-iio, SoapyPlutoSDR and kalibrate are now built
against a private libiio 0.26 (library only, /usr/libiio0/lib, found
through an rpath) and plutotx, a prebuilt program, gets the same rpath
from post-build.sh with patchelf.

Also pass CMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM to SoapyPlutoSDR: CMake 4 of the
new Buildroot refuses its cmake_minimum_required, so a clean build failed.

Tested on Pluto+ with the files copied to the running board:
SoapySDRUtil rate tests (RX 2.5 and 10 Msps, TX 2.5 Msps) give the same
rates as the real libiio 0.26, plutotx runs in high speed mode, kal scans.

Signed-off-by: Mario Behn <mario.behn@gmail.com>
